      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (52%):</strong> Diplomatic architecture holds formally — working groups convene, partial tranche releases continue — but nuclear and IAEA access impasses remain unresolved through August 16, extending the conflict into a negotiated stalemate with no resolution on enrichment or strait-clearing milestones.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (28%):</strong> Nuclear Affairs working group convenes before July 18 (F9 YES), produces a framework enrichment-level agreement by August 16 (F12 YES), and Hormuz commercial transits recover through insurance-market clearance to ≥50/day by August 3 (F10 YES) — the three necessary conditions for a substantive MOU implementation track.</p>
