        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iran's Supreme National Security Council issued a formal charter on July 3 clarifying that Mojtaba Khamenei holds no official deliberative role in SNSC proceedings during the interregnum. Mojtaba Khamenei's July 1 address, broadcast in full by IRNA and Tasnim and repeated across IRIB's July 2 evening programs, described the nuclear and missile programs as "national assets belonging to the Iranian people, not subject to foreign negotiation." No SNSC statement addressed the Islamabad MOU's working-group structure by name; Kayhan's front page through July 3 carried no reference to the Doha session or working-group calendar. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>MFA spokesperson Esmaeil Baghaei maintained bifurcated messaging through July 3: formal statements affirm MOU implementation "proceeding on schedule," while backgrounders to Iran International and al-Monitor described the Nuclear Affairs working group calendar as "not finalized." Deputy FM Gharibabadi confirmed four working groups (Nuclear Affairs, Hormuz Transit, Sanctions Relief, and Implementation Verification) formally designated by name at Doha July 1-2, but provided no convening dates for any group. The rial-dollar parallel-market rate closed at approximately 680,000 rial per dollar on July 3, stable over five consecutive trading days, which market participants attributed to MOU-implementation expectations. → supports <span class="cite">F9</span>, <span class="cite">F11</span>, <span class="cite">F12</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

